# HP Pro c640 Chromebook (Google Dratini / Hatch) Keyboard Top-Row Mapping
# Matches both standard Google Coreboot DMI strings and OEM HP DMI tables
#
# Scancodes inferred on real Dratini hardware (2026-10-31) from EVIOCGKEY
# key state plus the standard AT scancode->keycode table, then verified with
# EVIOCGKEYCODE on /dev/input/event2:
#   EVIOCGKEYCODE /dev/input/event2 -> 0x3b..0x44 = keycode 59..68 (KEY_F1..F10)
#   EVIOCGKEY while pressing brightness/mute BEFORE the fix -> KEY_F6/F7/F8,
#   which via the AT standard table corresponds to scancodes 0x40-0x42.
# EVIOCGKEY reports post-hwdb keycodes, not raw MSC_SCAN, so these are
# inferences from the AT table rather than direct scancode captures. Confirm
# the raw value with plain `evtest` (do NOT pass --grab) or with this repo's
# `--scan` mode after stopping keyd (`sudo systemctl stop keyd`); when done run
# `sudo systemctl start keyd` to restore the service.
# In other words this machine's top row behaves like the *standard AT* F1-F10,
# not the ChromeOS action scancodes (0xea/0xe9/0xe7/0x91/0x92/...) that
# 60-keyboard.hwdb-style snippets use for some other Chromebooks. Mapping
# 0x3b-0x44 is therefore what actually changes the behaviour here; the old
# 0xea-0xb0 block never matched a real key press and was dead code.
#
# These inferred scancodes are used on this Dratini only. The mapping is applied
# exclusively via the explicit DMI entries listed below (Dratini and the HP
# Pro c640); it is NOT verified for any other Hatch-based board. On real
# Dratini, "Hatch" appears in the product family (pfa), not the product name
# (pn), so no wildcard pn*Hatch* match is needed. Raw scancodes on other
# machines must be captured separately (e.g. with evtest without --grab)
# before adding any model-specific stanza.

evdev:atkbd:dmi:bvn*:bvr*:bd*:svnGoogle*:pn*Dratini*:pvr*
evdev:atkbd:dmi:bvn*:bvr*:bd*:svnGoogle*:pn*dratini*:pvr*
evdev:atkbd:dmi:bvn*:bvr*:bd*:svnHP*:pnHP*Pro*c640*Chromebook*:pvr*
evdev:atkbd:dmi:bvn*:bvr*:bd*:svnHP*:pn*c640*:pvr*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3b=back
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3c=forward
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3d=refresh
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3e=f11
 KEYBOARD_KEY_3f=scale
 KEYBOARD_KEY_40=brightnessdown
 KEYBOARD_KEY_41=brightnessup
 KEYBOARD_KEY_42=mute
 KEYBOARD_KEY_43=volumedown
 KEYBOARD_KEY_44=volumeup
 KEYBOARD_KEY_db=leftmeta
